SAMPLE_CONCEPTUAL_MODEL = """
Final Conceptual Data Model: Cloud FinOps Star Schema																									
																					
1. Model Selection and Structure																									
Component	Rationale (Meeting Sabre's Requirements)																								
Model Type	Dimensional Model (Star Schema). The highly normalized legacy EDW must be denormalized to achieve the required P90 dashboard load time (sub-20 seconds).																								
Granularity	Atomic Line-Item Level (Billing_Transaction_Ledger) and Hourly Time-Series (Utilizaton). This supports both reconciliation and deep anomaly detection.																								
Design Principle	Conformed Dimensions: All core dimensions (SKU, SERVICE, ORGANIZATION) must be consistent across the entire multi-cloud estate, enabling the Cross-Cloud Cost Allocation goal.																								
																									
2. Blueprint Mapping: Fact Tables (Data Tables)																									
The model uses the atomic Billing_Transaction_Ledger as the primary Transaction Fact and adds aggregated facts for performance.																									
Target Fact Table	Source Table Mapping (Source DDL)	Key Metrics Supported																							
FACT_DAILY_USAGE (Transaction)	Billing_Transaction_Ledger_Table (Core), Transaction_Credit_Item_Table	Total Monthly Cloud Spend, Unit Cost Metrics (cost/usage), Total Cost.																							
FACT_MONTHLY_AGGREGATE (Aggregate)	Aggregated from Billing_Transaction_Ledger_Table	Actual vs. Budget Variance (Supports fast historical trending and monthly summaries).																							
FACT_COMPLEX_PRICING (Bridge)	Account_SKU_Price_Rule, Account_Price_Tier_Table, Consumption_Model_Rule_Table	Models the M:M relationship between Dim_Account and Dim_Pricing elements to capture the negotiated effective rate.																							
																									
3. Blueprint Mapping: Dimension Tables (Master & Data Tables)																									
All dimensions are designed as wide, denormalized tables to simplify user queries and optimize Looker/Looker Studio performance.																									
Target Dimension Table	Source Table Mapping (Source DDL)	SCD Type Requirement																							
DIM_ORGANIZATION	Project_Profile_Table (Master), Project_Ancestor_Node_Table (Data Table)	SCD Type 2. Mandatory for tracking changes to business_unit and workload (Historical Cost Accountability).																							
DIM_PRODUCT	Service_SKU_Table (Master), Product_Taxonomy_Table (Data Table)	SCD Type 2. Captures changes to product definitions, descriptions, and taxonomy mappings.																							
DIM_RESOURCE	Resource_Inventory_Table (Master), Resource_Tag_Table (Data Table)	SCD Type 2. Necessary for resources where the location or environment changes over time.																							
DIM_LOCATION	Geo_Taxonomy_Table (Data Table)	SCD Type 1. Geography attributes (Region, Zone) are typically static lookups.																							
																									
4. Requirement Integration (Compliance & Performance)																									
Non-Functional Requirement	Implementation Strategy in the DDM																								
Query Performance SLO (sub-20s)	Achieved via Star Schema (denormalization) and the use of FACT_MONTHLY_AGGREGATE tables, allowing dashboards to query pre-summarized data.																								
RLS (Row-Level Security)	Implemented on the DIM_ORGANIZATION table. BigQuery RLS policies will restrict access to Fact tables based on the user's mapped business_unit or workload in the DIM_ORGANIZATION table.																								
SCD Type 2 Tracking	Applied to DIM_ORGANIZATION to satisfy the mandatory requirement for historical cost accountability when business_unit or workload changes. Also applied to PRODUCT and PRICING to preserve cost context.																								
Granularity (Hourly/Line-Item)	The model retains the atomic billing line-item in FACT_DAILY_USAGE and links to the DIM_TIME table for the required hourly time-series analysis (e.g., container cost allocation).																								
"""


